  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday Night through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1115 AM CST Thu Nov 12 2026\n\nShowers diminish Friday night and cold air will be settled into\nMiddle TN. This will bring a cold night with lows in the mid 20s\nto around 30s. Weak troughing will linger over the area on\nSaturday but we will see rising heights helping highs to push back\ninto the 50s. Saturday night will likely be the coldest night with\nlows in the mid 20s, much of the area will see a hard freeze.\nSunday into early next week an upper level ridge will build in\nfrom the west. This will bring a gradual warming trend to our\nhighs with them getting back into the low to mid 60s by the middle\nof the week. The air mass will be dry and that will keep the cold\nnights around with lows in the 20s to lower 30s. With a ridge in\nplace and strong high pressure sitting to our north we will remain\ndry with no precip chances.",
